            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "From dev-test:\n```\n- `NVIM_LUA_NOTRACK` (F) (D): disable reference counting of Lua objects\n```\n\nPreviously a neovim instance was launched as an LS (I have no idea why) with attaching disabled. My guess that it was just a dummy process and since we didn't care about the process itself, NVIM_LUA_NOTRACK probably has been set for performance reasons. This is purely my theory though.\n\nI needed attach/detach enabled for the test so I replaced that setup with the configuration from pull diagnostics tests (I assumed since they are more recent, this way of configuring a mock server is more \"up to date\").\n\nIt's not a process but just a mock server so it doesn't need env afaict.\n\nP.S. I'll remove textDocument/diagnostic handler since it's not needed when testing push diagnostics.",
