            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Right, the diagnostics module is a bit of a black sheep compared to the other ones.\n\n(For posterity): many LSP servers do not support \"pull\" diagnostics (so `textDocument/diagnostic` support is _false). This means that even though diagnostics are enabled, the capability framework will not attach/detach to buffers. However, the `publishDiagnostics` (push) path can still create push namespaces for buffers that are open in the editor.\n\nSo yeah, this is correct here (unfortunately, feels leaky to me) because the client itself detaching still needs to clear the \"push\" diagnostics for all those buffers that don't have any capability tracking on them which is just for pull, like you said.\n\nThere _could_ be a future improvement to capability where we let it attach if any N methods are supported, and then we could attach/detach if `textDocument/publishDiagnostics` is supported but we'd go into \"push\" mode by default.",
            "commit_id": "dc0e2ece718543d5c5fa213c452008726e59112c",
            "created_at": "2026-07-08T14:14:35Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -1436,6 +1436,8 @@ function Client:_on_detach(bufnr)\n     end\n   end\n \n+  vim.diagnostic.reset(vim.lsp.diagnostic.get_namespace(self.id, false), bufnr)",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40634#discussion_r3544684844",
